{"author":"schacon+claude-opus@gmail.com","body":"MOP-UP round 1: 200/236 (commit 12bbdd9 on grit-t5-progress). Fixed test 154 'incremental repack fails when bitmaps are requested': repack.rs now enforces builtin/repack.c:231 guard (write_bitmaps>0 && !full_repack && !write_midx -> die 'Incremental repacks are incompatible with bitmap indexes'). No regressions (t7700 still 36/47). Remaining 35 all require a REAL pack-bitmap reader/writer (grit writes 0-byte .bitmap placeholders): trace2 num_selected/num_maximal_commits (5/81/162), pack-reused progress (47/123/204), truncated/corrupt .bitmap detection needing real content (68/69/77/144/145/153/225/226/234/236), pack.usebitmaps=false delta suppression (71/147/228), bitmap delta-reuse (72/148/229), test-tool bitmap list-commits + preferBitmapTips (73-75 etc), 'opened/ignoring extra bitmap' trace2 (76/152/233), boundary-vs-classic traversal trace2 (156), lookup-table writing trace2 (235). ewah_bitmap.rs has a serialize/deserialize core but the full writer (commit selection, headers, type/xor/name-hash/lookup chunks) + reader + trace2 instrumentation is a multi-day feature; left for a dedicated bitmap ticket. Cannot close."}